Provides: x-terminal-emulator
Description: terminal emulator that behaves like a piece of hardware
 The picture is a curved tube. Phosphor keeps glowing after the pixel
 goes dark, bloom spills off bright type, and a scan line travels the
 glass. Around it sits a chassis with a numbered channel bank down one
 side. A session is picked by digit rather than read off a row of tabs,
 and switching channels degausses the way the original hardware did.
 .
 The terminal owns an SSH connection of its own, carrying several
 sessions as numbered channels on the bank, and speaks tmux control
 mode so a remote session's windows arrive as those channels too.
